<!-- Every localization should specify the direction of the language, -->
<!-- there is no assumed default.  Left-to-right is "ltr" and         -->
<!-- right-to-left is "rtl".  Provide these exactly as written since  -->
<!-- they can migrate untouched into output (e.g. HTML).              -->

<!-- Every localization should specify two "styles" for how       -->
<!-- primary/outer quote marks are given (double quotes in        -->
<!-- English) and how secondary/inner quote marks are given       -->
<!-- (single quotes in English).  Here are the extant styles      -->
<!-- and crude Unicode versions of how they might look:           -->
<!--                                                              -->
<!--     english-single          ‘word’                           -->
<!--     english-double          “word”                           -->
<!--     angle-single            ‹word›                           -->
<!--     angle-double            «word»                           -->
<!--     angle-single-space      ‹ word ›                         -->
<!--     angle-double-space      « word »                         -->
<!--     down-up-single          ‚word’                           -->
<!--     down-up-double          „word”                           -->
<!--                                                              -->
<!-- Maintainers: please use the  pretext-dev  group to discuss   -->
<!-- what is best for your language.  If a style exists, then it  -->
<!-- is just a simple edit of the default English values.  New    -->
<!-- styles require Unicode values and LaTeX macros to be         -->
<!-- implemented, work which RAB can do easily.  Examples in the  -->
<!-- sample article can be updated with new languages/countries,  -->
<!-- or created with iconic quotes from the specific language.    -->
<!-- The table at Wikipedia is not a bad thing to consult, even   -->
<!-- if it seems to have some inaccuracies.                       -->
<!--                                                              -->
<!--     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quotation_mark             -->

